          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          An electric zero turn mower is a battery with a deck attached. Speed, cut height and deck options are close to identical across brands, so the buying decision comes down to one ratio: kilowatt-hours of battery against acres of grass. Get that right and you mow quietly, with no fuel and no oil changes. Get it wrong and you finish the last corner with a push mower.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="what-changes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What an Electric Zero Turn Changes (and What It Does Not)
          </h2>

          <p>
            An electric zero turn mower swaps the engine, belts and hydrostatic transaxles for a battery pack and three to five electric motors: one on each rear wheel and one or more on the blades. That changes the ownership experience far more than it changes the cut. There is no oil to change, no carburetor to gum up over winter, no spark plug, no fuel stabilizer, and no belt squealing across a deck pulley. You turn a key, push the blade switch, and the motors spin up in a second or two. The noise is mostly blade whoosh, which matters if you mow at 7 a.m. or share a fence line.
          </p>

          <p>
            What it does not change is physics. A zero turn still steers with its drive wheels, so it still slides on a wet slope, still scalps on rolling ground if the deck is too wide, and still needs sharp blades and a level deck to cut well. Battery mowers also add one new limit a gas mower never had: a hard ceiling on how much grass you can cut before you stop. Gas mowers run out of fuel too, but refilling takes two minutes. Refilling a 4 kWh battery takes hours.
          </p>

          <p>
            That is why the buying decision is almost entirely about battery capacity versus acreage. Deck width, speed and cut height ranges are close to identical across the electric models on this page; every one of them tops out around 8 mph and cuts between 1.5 and 4.5 inches. The real differences are how many kilowatt-hours ride under the seat, how fast they recharge, and what it will cost to replace them in year six or seven.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are still deciding between a zero turn and a lawn tractor at all, read our <a href="/zero-turn-vs-riding-mower/">zero turn vs riding mower</a> comparison first. If you have already decided on a zero turn and want the full gas field compared, our main <a href="/best-zero-turn-mower/">best zero turn mower</a> guide covers the Toro, Husqvarna, Ariens and Deere machines. This page is narrower on purpose: battery zero turns only, judged on the numbers that decide whether one charge finishes your lawn.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">THE SHORT VERSION</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Buy watt-hours, not horsepower-equivalent claims.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Every brand quotes a gas-equivalent horsepower figure. None of them is standardised. Total pack capacity in watt-hours, divided by your acreage, tells you far more about whether the mower finishes the job.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The 5 Best Electric Zero Turn Mowers, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            We compared the battery zero turns sold on Amazon from EGO and Greenworks on total nominal battery capacity, the manufacturer's acreage rating, charge time, deck width and the cost of keeping the batteries going. Capacity figures are our arithmetic from each kit's voltage and amp-hour ratings; acreage and charge times are attributed to the manufacturer or retailer listings that publish them.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
