        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy an electric zero turn if you mow one to three-and-a-half acres of actual turf every week and can give the charger its own outlet. For most of those yards, the EGO ZT5207L is the one to get: about 4 kWh of battery, a 52-inch deck and packs that also run the rest of EGO's tools. Under an acre and a half, the 42-inch ZT4204L does the job for less.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Size the battery, not the horsepower claim. Divide the kit's watt-hours by your mowed acreage, plan on 70% of the rated coverage, and price out the replacement packs before you buy. If the numbers do not work for your lawn, a gas zero turn is still the better tool, and that is a fine answer.
